WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.470
Four sketches with no numbers.

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.850
A straight line.

3
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.050
A U-shape.

4
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.400
An S-shape.

5
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:09.060
And a curve in two separate pieces.

6
00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.960
Beside them, four shuffled equations.

7
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.630
Y equals two x minus one.

8
00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.430
Y equals x squared minus four.

9
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.070
Y equals minus x cubed.

10
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.600
Y equals four over x.

11
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.700
Could you match them up without
plotting a single point?

12
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.880
Or do you need a table of values?

13
00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.930
Or just the biggest number?

14
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.460
In this mission, you'll learn the shapes.

15
00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.860
A linear graph is a straight line.

16
00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.010
A quadratic is a parabola.

17
00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:41.610
You'll meet the S-shaped cubic, and the
reciprocal graph with its asymptotes.

18
00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:46.520
And you'll read roots and y-intercepts,
where a curve crosses the axes.

19
00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:51.330
Your mission: match the four graphs
to their equations, without plotting.
